  coachNote: "Monday check: which office sale is the campaign, and is the Snapshot's Sold section ticked with dates, plus the Buyers calls? Have the associate run the Just Sold knock on you twice, once on a no, once on a yes. Listen for the real reason, the four buyer qualifiers, the pause after the ask, Jess's exact NO close, and a day and time on the yes. Good looks like about 20 geo data, 200 calls, 3 appraisals, first listing in hand. Sit the three-question debrief with a number per avenue. The ratio to watch: Just Sold conversations per appraisal booked, against the cold-call ratio. If warm is not clearly better, the ask is being softened or the silence filled."
